      "citations": [
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00657",
          "explanation": "Family surfaced a case-specific misconception/uncertainty about reduced oxygen implying discharge readiness.",
          "quote": "不等于马上好了"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00813",
          "explanation": "Doctor explicitly corrected the misconception in simple language.",
          "quote": "绝不等于“已经好了”"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "lite_evt_00956",
          "explanation": "Family teach-back showed the corrected mental model changed intended behavior.",
          "quote": "有突然更喘、人不对劲、胸痛这些就按铃"
        }
      ],
      "completion": "complete",
      "explanation": "HO1 was triggered by repeated family concern that improvement, oxygen reduction, or falling inflammatory markers might mean the patient was essentially ready for discharge. The doctor named and corrected that misconception, linked it to the patient’s activity-related dyspnea/oxygen need, and the family later restated that they would not treat it as cured and would escalate danger signs.",
